2. **Saltatory Conensation**: This occurs in the myeninated neural cells. The membrane is only exposed in the neural membranes at the neural regions called nodes of Ranner. The electrical charge ""jumps"" from one neuron to the other, leading to a faster conduction of the electrical signal. This process is faster because the electrical charge does not have to move across the entire membrane.

