   c. Temperature and solvation: Changes in the solvent's properties with temperature (e.g., viscosity, dielectric constant) can also affect the zeta potential.

In summary, the zeta potential of silica nanoparticles is highly sensitive to pH and less sensitive to temperature. The pH of the solution determines the surface charge of the nanoparticles, while temperature can affect the zeta potential by influencing the ionic strength, specific adsorption, and solvation properties of the system.
