3. Reactor residence time: The reactor residence time is the average amount of time that the reactants are in the reactor. Longer residence times can lead to higher conversion of the reactants, but may also result in the formation of by-products or degradation of the surfactant. The optimal residence time will depend on the specific reaction and the desired product quality.

