","The **geometric mean of the root mean square (RMS) transfer factor (TF) for \(^{137}\text{Cs}\) from soil to polished rice** is a measure of the average transfer efficiency of \(^{137}\text{Cs}\) from the soil to the soil-green-green-polished rice. This value is typically used in the SAR (Specific Activity Ratio) method for the assessment of internal exposure to radioactivity. 

The **standard value** for the **geometric mean** of the \(^{137}\text{Cs}\) transfer factor from soil to polished rice is **10\(^{1.5}\)**. This is equivalent to:

