     - Let M_u be the molecular weight of the unknown solute.
     - Moles of unknown solute = mass / molecular weight = 0.6216 g / M_u
     - Kilograms of CCl₄ = 50 g / 1000 g/kg = 0.050 kg
     - Molality of unknown solute solution (m_unknown) = (0.6216 g / M_u) / 0.050 kg

   - Use the boiling point elevation formula to find M_u:
