1. **\( \text{CuS} \):** \( \text{Cu}^{2+} \) is less soluble than \( \text{Ni}^{2+} \), \( \text{Hg}^{2+} \), or \( \text{Mn}^{2+} \). \( \text{CuS} \) is insoluble and precipitates.
2. **\( \text{HgS} \):** \( \text{Hg}^{2+} \) is less soluble than \( \text{Ni}^{2+} \) or \( \text{Mn}^{2+} \). \( \text{HgS} \) is insoluble and precipitates.
3. **\( \text{MnS} \):** \( \text{Mn}^{2+} \) is less soluble than \( \text{Ni}^{2+} \). \( \text{MnS} \) is insoluble and precipitates.
