6. **pH below the IEP**: As the pH decreases below the IEP, more surface groups tend to protonate, resulting in a net positive charge on the particles. This leads to an increase in the positive zeta potential.

7. **Effect of ionic strength**: The effect of pH on the zeta potential is also influenced by the ionic strength of the solution. Higher ionic strength will cause the zeta potential to decrease due to the increased shielding of the surface charge by the ions in the solution. This is known as the depacking effect.

In summary, the pH of a solution affects the zeta potential of colloidal particles by altering the surface charge of the particles, which in turn is influenced by the ionic strength of the solution.
