The CuCO₂ complex consists of a copper (Cu) atom interacting with a CO₂ molecule. The geometry of the complex depends on how the Cu atom binds to the CO₂ molecule. CO₂ is linear in its free state (O=C=O), but when it coordinates to a metal like Cu, it can form a bent or angled structure.

