1. Si doping in TiO2 nanoparticles: The Si atoms can substitute Ti atoms in the TiO2 lattice, forming Si-Ti-O clusters or Si-rich phases. The presence of Si can lead to the formation of Si-rich phases, such as SiO2 or TiSi2, which can act as impurities or impurities with different properties.

