**Part 1: $f$ has the quamin property at $x^* \implies \nabla f(x^*)(y - x^*) \geq 0$ for all $y \in \mathcal{U}$**
Suppose $f$ has the quamin property at $x^*$. This means that:
\[
\lim_{y \to x^*} \frac{f(y) - f(x^*)}{\|y - x^*\}} \geq 0.
\]
Since $f$ is Frchet differentiable at $x^*$, there exists $\alpha = \nabla f(x^*) \in \mathcal{X}^*$ such that for all $h \in \mathcal{X}$:
\[
