\[
\lim_{\text{deg}h \to 0} \frac{f(x^* + h) - f(x^*)}{\|h\}} = \alpha(h).
\]
Since $f$ has the quamin property, we have:
\[
\alpha(h) \geq 0 \quad \text{for all } h \in \mathcal{X}.
