b) **Cross-sectional**: This is a **cross-sectional** design because data on eating habits and general health are measured at a single point in time. The relationship between these variables is assessed simultaneously.

c) **Propective**: This is a **proive** design because the researchers are following a group of people over time, observing their exposure (e.g., eating and exchange practices) and then assessing the development of a particular outcome (cancer).

