Suppose the set of rational numbers in [0, 1] is denoted by $Q \cap [0, 1]$. For each $q \in Q \cap [0, 1]$, we can express it as a rational number in its lowest terms, i.e., $q = \frac{p}{n}$, where $p, n \in \mathbb{Z}$, $0 \leq p \leq n$, and $\text{gcd}(p, n) = 1$.

