$$\frac{3}{8}\pi = \frac{\theta}{360^\circ} \pi (1)^2$$
$$\frac{3}{8} = \frac{\theta}{360^\circ}$$
Solving for $\theta$, we get:
$$\theta = 360^\circ \cdot \frac{3}{8} = 45^\circ \cdot 3 = 135^\circ$$
The central angle of the unfolded diagram of this cone is $135^\circ$.

