\[
mv_0 + M \cdot 0 = mv_1 + Mv_2 \implies mv_0 = mv_1 + Mv_2 \implies v_1 = \frac{mv_0 - Mv_2}{m}
\]
Substituting \( v_1 \) into the equation \( v_2 - v_1 = -eV_0 \):
\[
v_2 - \frac{mv_0 - Mv_2}{m} = -eV_0 \implies \frac{mMv_2 - mv_0 + Mv_2}{m} = -eV_0 \implies (m + M)v_2 - mv_0 = -MEv_0
\]
Solving for \( v_2 \):
\[
v_2 = \frac{mv_0 - MEv_0}{m + M} = \frac{m - Me}{m + M} v_0
\]
Substituting \( v_2 \) back into the equation for \( v_1 \):
\[
v_1 = \frac{mv_0 - M \left( \frac{m - Me}{m + M} v_0 \right)}{m} = \frac{mv_0 - \frac{M(m - Me)v_0}{m + M}}{m} = \frac{m(m + M)v_0 - M(m - Me)v_0}{m(m + M)} = \frac{(m^2 + mM - mM + M^2 e) v_0}{m(m + M)} = \frac{(m^2 + M^2 e) v_0}{m(m + M)}
\]
