The effective index \(n_{\text{eff}}\) is the refractive index of the guide, which is the Ga\(_{0.2}\)Al_{0.8}As cladding in this case. Thus, \(n_{\text{eff}} = n_{\text{cladding}}\).

The given condition \(n_{\text{eff}} - n_f \approx 0.3\) implies \(n_{\text{eff}} - 1 \approx 0.3\), so \(n_{\text{eff}} \approx 1.3\).

