2. Thin film fabrication: Plasma-assisted chemical vapor deposition (PECVD) can be used to deposit thin films of materials such as silicon nitride, silicon oxide, and silicon-based materials for solar cells. These films can act as anti-reflection coatings, solar absorbers, or device junctions, improving the overall efficiency of the solar cell.

