   The area per particle is \(A = \pi (d/2)^2 = \pi (10^{-8}/2)^2 = 0.785 \times 10^{-16}\) m\(^2\).
   The center-to-center spacing is \(6 \times 10^{-8}\) m, so the area per particle is also \(N \times A = 6 \times 10^{-8}\).
