","To calculate the average radiation dose to the body tissue, we can use the following formula:

\[
\text{Absorbed Dose (Gy) = \frac{\text{Absorbed Energy (J)}}{\text{Mass of tissue (kg)}}
\]

Given:
- Absorbed energy = 0.12 J
- Mass of liver tissue = 1.6 kg

Substituting the values:
\[
\text{Absored Dose (Gy) = \frac{0.12 \text{ J}}{1.6 \text{ kg}} = 0.075 \text{ Gy}
\]

The absorbed dose is 0.75 Gy.

