\[
V_T = \sqrt{\frac{2E_g}{3}} - \frac{2\phi_F}{3} - \frac{1}{\pi} \cdot \frac{2\varepsilon_S}{\sqrt{2}} \ln\left(\frac{N_A}{N_D}\)
\]

where:
- \(E_g\) is the bandgap energy of silicon (\(1.12 \text{ eV}\))
- \(\phi_F\) is the Fermi potential
- \(\varepsilon_S\) is the permittivity of silicon (\(11.7 \text{ F/cm}\))
- \(N_A\) is the acceptor doping concentration (for p-type substrate)
- \(N_D\) is the donor doping concentration (in the region)

The change in threshold voltage \(\Delta V_T\) is given by the electric field in the region:

\[
