","To determine the entropy production rate \( \Pi_S \) for the rubbing of two balls, we use the Boltzmann's equation for entropy production:

\[
\Pi_S = \frac{F_{\text{fr}} v}{T}
\]

where \( F_{\text{fr}} \) is the friction force, \( v \) is the mean relative velocity, and \( T \) is the temperature. This equation arises from the Maxwell-Boltzmann distribution and the entropy of particles in equilibrium. The friction force does work, and this work is dissipated as heat due to the friction, increasing the system's entropy. The entropy production rate is proportional to the work done per unit time (power) and inversely proportional to the temperature.

Thus, the entropy production rate is:

\[
\Pi_S = \frac{F_{\text{fr}} v}{T}
