     - **c̄c̄ (c-quark-c̄ quark)**: ~27% (but these decay quickly into other quarks and leptons, making them more challenging to detect directly).
     - **μ⁺μ⁻ (μ-μ) and τ⁺τ⁻ (τ-τ)**: These leptons are heavier and thus have higher coupling to the Higgs.
     - **ūd̄, ūs, c̄s, c̄b, t̄b (other quark pairs)**: These have smaller quark masses and thus smaller contributions to the decay rate.
